            {
              "front": "What does the 'umask' value 022 establish?",
              "back": "Masks write permission for group and others; creates default files with 644 (rw-r--r--) and directories with 755 (rwxr-xr-x)."
            },
            {
              "front": "What is the difference between '$*' and '$@' in Bash?",
              "back": "Inside double quotes, \"$*\" expands to a single string with elements separated by IFS (\"$1 $2...\"), whereas \"$@\" expands to separate words (\"$1\" \"$2\"...)."
            },
            {
              "front": "What does 'kill -9' (SIGKILL) do that 'kill -15' (SIGTERM) cannot?",
              "back": "SIGKILL cannot be caught, handled, or ignored by a process; it forces immediate unconditional kernel termination."
            },
            {
              "front": "What is a Named Pipe (FIFO)?",
              "back": "A special file on disk (created with mkfifo) that provides bidirectional inter-process communication with FIFO semantics between unrelated processes."
            }
